# Keeps the build context small and keeps host state out of the image. Everything the backend
# image needs is copied explicitly in backend/Dockerfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
coverage
.git
.github
# Its *contents*, not the directory: Docker never traverses an excluded directory, so a `!`
# exception under `.devcontainer` would be silently inert — the re-inclusion below only works
# because the directory itself stays in the context.
.devcontainer/*
# The development CouchDB's configuration overlay is the exception. That image builds from the
# repository root so it can reach the base configuration it shares with production, which puts
# it under this file's rules; without this its COPY fails on a context that does not contain
# the file, and says only that the file is missing.
!.devcontainer/couchdb
!.devcontainer/couchdb/**
.playwright-mcp
e2e
packages/web
docs
*.log
.env
